WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.762
Please welcome Leslie Jordan.

2
00:00:01.762 --> 00:00:03.091
(audience applauds)
(claps) Leslie.

3
00:00:03.091 --> 00:00:04.989
And look at you two.

4
00:00:04.989 --> 00:00:07.460
You look so good, both of you.

5
00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:08.800
Oh, you look so good too.

6
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.141
You look, you look very proper

7
00:00:10.141 --> 00:00:12.500
in a little scarf, ascotty thing.

8
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:13.479
Well, I dressed.

9
00:00:13.479 --> 00:00:15.280
(audience laughs)
(Ross laughs)

10
00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:18.440
I'm just so excited to be speaking with you here today.

11
00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:19.700
I'm such a fan of yours,

12
00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:22.190
and especially what you've done

13
00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:23.550
and accomplished in 2020

14
00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:25.559
with putting yourself out there on social media.

15
00:00:25.559 --> 00:00:28.843
It's just been such a bright light for everyone.

16
00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:31.640
Well, it wasn't really planned.

17
00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:32.810
It just kinda happened.

18
00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:37.210 line:15%
I was stuck in Tennessee with my mom for the lockdown,

19
00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:40.900 line:15%
and I started doing Instagrams to pass the time.

20
00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:43.870 line:15%
I did two a day for 80 days, and I just,

21
00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:45.380
without even thinking it through.

22
00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:47.270
I didn't go anywhere near politics.

23
00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:49.490
I didn't go anywhere near religion.

24
00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:51.910
I just wanted to give people, you know,

25
00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:54.210
a place to go where they could just laugh.

26
00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:56.990
You know, people come up to me in grocery stores

27
00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:59.660
and say, "Oh, Mr. Jordan, I was stuck at home.

28
00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:02.170 line:15%
I got three kids, my husband, la la la.

29
00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:05.010 line:15%
I would come to you once a day just for a good laugh,

30
00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:06.150 line:15%
and I would look forward to it."

31
00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:07.900 line:15%
You know, you realize how important

32
00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:10.253
just comedy is, especially now,

33
00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:14.140
during all of this.
I completely agree.

34
00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.810
You are a national treasure,

35
00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:16.920
and you have made people,

36
00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:19.530
and that authenticity of putting it out there

37
00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:21.080
with those brilliant intentions

38
00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:23.840
is probably why it connected so much with everybody.

39
00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:25.050
So, thank you.

40
00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:26.810
Yeah, and 2020 was-
Well, you're welcome.

41
00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:28.030
It was so hard, Leslie.

42
00:01:28.030 --> 00:01:31.510
And every day, I know myself and millions of other people

43
00:01:31.510 --> 00:01:34.480
would go to your IG, just to feel better.

44
00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:35.960
So, thank you for what you gave us.

45
00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:36.870
Thank you, honey.

46
00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:37.713
That's so sweet.

47
00:01:37.713 --> 00:01:39.730
Leslie, would you be kind enough

48
00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:42.650
to join us in some headlines at the news desk?

49
00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:43.789
Absolutely.

50
00:01:43.789 --> 00:01:44.622
(audience claps)

51
00:01:44.622 --> 00:01:45.780
Oh, good, okay Ross.

52
00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:47.446
Take it away.
Okay, let's see, gotta talk.

53
00:01:47.446 --> 00:01:48.990
So many people are conducting

54
00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:50.920
radical hair experiments this year,

55
00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:53.737
because people growin' it out in quarantine.

56
00:01:53.737 --> 00:01:57.230
"Men's Health" says if you've ever mulled a mullet,

57
00:01:57.230 --> 00:01:58.680
the time is now.

58
00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:01.010
And celebs are showing off their (laughs) party tails

59
00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:02.820
from Miley Cyrus to Billie Eilish,

60
00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:05.960
and of course, country star Morgan Wallen rocks a mullet.

61
00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:08.426
And stylists say it is now the prime time

62
00:02:08.426 --> 00:02:09.920
for a mullet moment,

63
00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:11.280
'cause people have been growing their hair out,

64
00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:12.930
so you can trim the sides.

65
00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:14.350 line:15%
A mullet doesn't work for everybody.

66
00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:17.670 line:15%
I am pretty passionate that it, you know,

67
00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.010 line:15%
business in the front and,

68
00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:20.256 line:15%
poor life choices in the back.

69
00:02:20.256 --> 00:02:21.660 line:15%
Did we have a moment?
(Drew and Leslie laughing)

70
00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:25.000 line:15%
But this is what I would look like with a mullet, Drew.

71
00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.390 line:15%
I have to say, sorta hot.

72
00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:27.460 line:15%
Anyone else?

73
00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:28.900 line:15%
Ross, I'm in.

74
00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:29.733 line:15%
You're in?

75
00:02:29.733 --> 00:02:30.566 line:15%
Yeah.

76
00:02:30.566 --> 00:02:31.399 line:15%
Well, let's see what you would look like

77
00:02:31.399 --> 00:02:32.255 line:15%
in a mullet (laughs).

78
00:02:32.255 --> 00:02:33.088 line:15%
(Drew laughs)

79
00:02:33.088 --> 00:02:34.447 line:15%
Okay, Drew, I'm out (laughs).

80
00:02:35.990 --> 00:02:37.460 line:15%
And Leslie, we got you too.

81
00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:41.300 line:15%
Wow.
Oh, you look sweet.

82
00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:43.320 line:15%
Are you a mullet man, Leslie?

83
00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:45.030 line:15%
No, not at all.
No.

84
00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:47.180
I remember the very first mullet I saw,

85
00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:50.680
was probably Jane Fonda, believe it or not.

86
00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:51.513
For "Klute."
Oh, yes.

87
00:02:51.513 --> 00:02:53.290
She had that movie called "Klute."

88
00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:56.880
But see, back then, we called it the shag, I think.

89
00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:57.914
But it was a mullet.

90
00:02:57.914 --> 00:02:59.113
(laughs) It was a mullet.
Yeah.

91
00:02:59.113 --> 00:03:00.650
Everybody had the shag.

92
00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:02.090
But no, I never had that.

93
00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:04.430
I did, you know, I was,

94
00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:06.440
in 1969 I was 14.

95
00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:09.200
So all I wanted out of life was to be a hippie.

96
00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:10.880
And I had all this hair,

97
00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:13.350
and my hair was kinda red, big.

98
00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:17.186 line:15%
I looked like a little rock and roll troll doll.

99
00:03:17.186 --> 00:03:19.773 line:15%
(Drew and Ross laughing)

100
00:03:19.773 --> 00:03:21.710 line:15%
I'm this big with all that hair (laughs).

101
00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:24.330
By the way, if you can get us a picture of that, Leslie,

102
00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:25.847
we would be thrilled.
We would love to see that.

103
00:03:25.847 --> 00:03:26.947
Oh, I don't, (indistinct) I burned 'em.

104
00:03:26.947 --> 00:03:29.870
Oh, well, I bet you looked so good.

105
00:03:29.870 --> 00:03:31.410
Okay, well, sticking with style news,

106
00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:34.957
let's turn to the latest in furry fashion.

107
00:03:34.957 --> 00:03:37.210 line:15%
"InStyle" reports that you can now buy

108
00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:39.090 line:15%
UGG Boots for your dog.

109
00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:40.330 line:15%
Finally.
Yep, that's right.

110
00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:43.500 line:15%
Put a pug in an UGG.
(Ross laughs)

111
00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:45.485 line:15%
These booties come in a classic tan,

112
00:03:45.485 --> 00:03:47.960 line:15%
and in a black with green trim.

113
00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:49.620
Leslie, do you have a little doggie?

114
00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:52.070
Would you put them in UGGs?
I don't have a doggie,

115
00:03:52.070 --> 00:03:53.640
and I don't get UGGs.

116
00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:54.831 line:15%
Don't your feet sweat?

117
00:03:54.831 --> 00:03:55.664 line:15%
(Ross laughs)

118
00:03:55.664 --> 00:03:56.497 line:15%
No.
There was Pam Anderson,

119
00:03:56.497 --> 00:03:57.844 line:15%
runnin' on the beach.

120
00:03:57.844 --> 00:03:59.732 line:15%
I thought, I bet her feet stink.

121
00:03:59.732 --> 00:04:00.565 line:15%
(Ross laughs)

122
00:04:00.565 --> 00:04:03.370 line:15%
I don't think I'm a UGGer.

123
00:04:03.370 --> 00:04:04.640 line:15%
Well, listen.
I'm not a UGGy guy.

124
00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:06.270 line:15%
I have three dogs, and they're,

125
00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:07.720 line:15%
you know, we live in Palm Springs.

126
00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:08.880 line:15%
And coming here to New York,

127
00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:10.660
these dogs, their feet are cold.

128
00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:12.112
So I want a rush order.

129
00:04:12.112 --> 00:04:14.214
Oh, there you go.
Don't take pause (laughs).

130
00:04:14.214 --> 00:04:15.930
I'm kidding.
Don't pause today.

131
00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:17.010
Don't pause.

132
00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:18.830
You know what's also really helpful

133
00:04:18.830 --> 00:04:19.900
about these UGGs,

134
00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:22.930
is that in East Coast places,

135
00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:25.200
it's not something I knew growing up in California.

136
00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:26.724
They salt the roads,

137
00:04:26.724 --> 00:04:31.724
and that salt actually burns the dogs' paws.

138
00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:33.210
It's really toxic for them.

139
00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:34.770
It burns right through the skin.

140
00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:35.840
So you'll see a dog,

141
00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:38.070
so the UGG Boots are really smart for that,

142
00:04:38.070 --> 00:04:41.230
and then Robin, she is really heavy into design,

143
00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:42.260
and was like, "You know what?

144
00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:44.370
I have lighter carpets, and I put my dogs in them

145
00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:46.370
so they don't ruin them when we take them outside."

146
00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:47.203
Mm, mm.

147
00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:50.320
Well, there you go.

148
00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:52.020
So, don't burn your dog,

149
00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:54.620
and keep your carpets clean.
(Ross laughs)

150
00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:56.420
Leslie, and you would look cute with a little dog,

151
00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:57.460
I gotta say.

152
00:04:57.460 --> 00:04:58.630
Oh, I've had dogs over the years.

153
00:04:58.630 --> 00:04:59.641
I've always had big dogs.

154
00:04:59.641 --> 00:05:01.370
I love Labs.

155
00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:02.203
But then again,

156
00:05:02.203 --> 00:05:04.523
I went through a long Jack Russell Terrier phase.

157
00:05:04.523 --> 00:05:05.356
Mm-hm.

158
00:05:05.356 --> 00:05:06.500
I had little Earl for 18 years.

159
00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:08.559
Little Earl.
I had a little Jack Russell.

160
00:05:08.559 --> 00:05:10.260
Oh.
He was a criminal, honey.

161
00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:11.571
Had a rap sheet long as your arm.

162
00:05:11.571 --> 00:05:12.404
(audience laughs)
(Ross laughs)

163
00:05:12.404 --> 00:05:15.100
I couldn't, I never even paper trained him.

164
00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:18.390
He wouldn't even (laughs) paper train.

165
00:05:18.390 --> 00:05:19.880
His dog is a criminal (laughs).

166
00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:21.170
I love it.

167
00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:24.540
Well, you have stolen our hearts, Leslie Jordan,

168
00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:27.710
for many years, and you really propped us up

169
00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:29.140
in the year we needed it most.

170
00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:30.531
Thank you for joining us.
Well, you both

171
00:05:30.531 --> 00:05:31.364
are just precious,

172
00:05:31.364 --> 00:05:32.560
and I wish you the best
(audience applauds)

173
00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:33.940
with this show.

174
00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:35.360
Well, thank you Leslie.

175
00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:39.027 line:15%
(upbeat contemporary music)

